description:
In decode.rs, the begin line parsing has a dead code path.

The begin_idx search loop (lines 58-66) finds a line index only when the line starts with 'begin' (case-insensitive) followed by whitespace or '-'. The found line is stored in begin_line.

Lines 91-94 then tokenize begin_line by ASCII whitespace. Since begin_line was found precisely because it starts with 'begin', tokens will always be non-empty and tokens[0] will always be 'begin' (case-insensitively).

The check on lines 96-99:
  if tokens.is_empty() || !tokens[0].eq_ignore_ascii_case(b"begin") {
      return Err(UuError::InvalidBeginLine { ... });
  }
can never be true given the invariant established by the search loop. This is dead code.

Impact: No correctness issue, but the dead branch creates confusion ('why would begin_idx point to a non-begin line?') and wastes cognitive overhead during future maintenance. It also slightly misleads readers into thinking this is a reachable error path.

Fix: Remove the guard on lines 96-99, or add a debug_assert! instead of a runtime check to document the invariant without dead production code.
